| Data tables | `tables-datatables.html`, `tables-listjs.html` |
| Forms | `forms-elements.html`, `forms-layouts.html`, `forms-validation.html`, `forms-wizard.html` |
| Modals / alerts | `ui-modals.html`, `ui-alerts.html`, `advance-ui-sweetalerts.html` |
| Profile / settings | `pages-profile.html`, `pages-profile-settings.html` |
| Public marketing (if needed) | `landing.html` (adapt branding to CSFP/APICS) |

## Required implementation patterns

- Shell: `#layout-wrapper`, `#page-topbar`, `.app-menu` / sidebar, `.main-content`, `.page-content`, footer — as in Velzon.
- CSS/JS stack from template: Bootstrap + Velzon `app.min.css` / `bootstrap.min.css` / `icons.min.css` / `custom.min.css`, `layout.js`, `app.js`, and libs as the demo uses.
- Asset URLs: prefer `asset('master/assets/...')` so paths stay relative to this project.
- Keep enterprise SPA rules for **behavior**: Axios `/api/v1`, no full-page reload on CRUD, toast for success/error, Swal for confirmations, DataTables where listing, audit on mutations.
- Branding: replace Velzon logos/titles with **APICS / CSFP OCBO**; keep Velzon visual language (Poppins/Public Sans, cards, badges, sidebar).
- Responsive: preserve Velzon’s responsive sidebar/topbar behavior; still verify device matrix (320px→1920+, Apple Safari).

## Do not

- Rebuild auth/admin pages with a custom Tailwind-only look that ignores `public/master`.
- Copy huge HTTrack demos verbatim into Blade without stripping unused widgets — **reuse structure + needed parts**.
- Hardcode absolute machine paths; always use project-relative `public/master`.
- Mix conflicting UI kits on the same screen (e.g. heavy custom Tailwind cards beside Velzon layout without adapting).

## When unsure

Open `public/master/` demos first, pick the closest page, then implement APICS content inside that shell. If no demo fits, extend from `pages-starter.html` using Velzon components from `ui-*.html` / `forms-*.html` / `tables-*.html`.
